auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
}

docs {
  # agent-1o1-ai API

  Internal V1 API (bearer/Passport auth) plus the Public V1 API (API-key auth).

  ## Response envelope

  Every Internal V1 response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data }`
  on success, `{ success, statusCode, message, errors? }` on failure (`errors`
  present for 422 validation failures). Actual payloads always live under
  `data` — e.g. login's tokens are at `data.tokens`, not top-level. Endpoints
  that return no body (delete, logout, revoke) still respond `204 No Content`
  with no envelope at all.

  ## Auth flow

  1. Run `auth/Register` or `auth/Login`. Their post-response script stores
     `accessToken` and `refreshToken` as collection variables.
  2. Every other Internal V1 request inherits collection-level bearer auth
     and automatically uses `{{accessToken}}`.
  3. Requests under `workspaces/{workspace}/...` also need a `workspaceId`
     variable set (see the `local` environment) — set it after creating or
     listing a workspace.
  4. Public V1 requests (`public/...`) use a workspace API key instead —
     set `{{apiKey}}` from `workspaces/api-keys/Create Api Key`.
  5. The webhook endpoints under `Webhooks` use neither: the token in the
     URL is the whole auth story. See that folder's requests.

  ## Resource ID variables

  Most folders' `Create` requests store the new record's ID in a collection
  variable, so the rest of that folder works without hand-editing paths:
  `workflowId`, `versionId`, `runId`, `triggerId`, `triggerToken`,
  `builderSessionId`, `agentId`, `agentSessionId`, `toolBindingId`,
  `skillId`, `skillReferenceId`, `skillScriptId`, and `planId` (set by
  `Billing/Plans - List`). Running a folder top to bottom fills them in
  as it goes.

  Two have no `Create` to populate them and must be set by hand from a
  response body: `approvalId` (from a run parked on an approval node) and
  `waitToken` (from the callback URL a Wait node hands out).

  ## Suggested order

  `Auth` → `Workspaces` (create one, then an API key) → `Workflows` →
  `Workflow Builder` (draft a graph) → `Workflows/Versions - Publish` →
  `Runs`. `Agents`, `Skills`, and `Triggers` are independent of that
  chain apart from needing `workspaceId` — though attaching a workflow
  tool or pointing a trigger at a workflow needs `workflowId` too.
}
